    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the changes I made to replace the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel`:\n\n## Changes\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` schema property (string enum GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE) with `membershipLevel`, an `integer` (1\u20133, readOnly). Since the DTO is generated from this spec at build time, this removes `membershipTier`/`MembershipTierEnum` from `OwnerDto` and adds `membershipLevel`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced the `@Mapping` target and the `membershipTier(...)` method with `membershipLevel(...)`, computing: start at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3. Removed the now-unused GOLD-household logic (`isGoldHousehold`, `GOLD_HOUSEHOLD_SIZE`) since the household-tenure path is reserved for level 4 and not derived here.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 The create audit line now records `membershipLevel` instead of the tier. I build the DTO before logging and read the level from it, so the audited value is exactly the one returned in the response. Updated the audit logger's Javadoc to match.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New test `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` passes \u2014 an owner with an email and a unique name (namesakeCount 0) gets `membershipLevel = 3` (1 + email + namesake0, capped at 3).\n- Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n- The audit output confirms the new format: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-LEV-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-12 membershipLevel=3`.\n\nOne note on a judgment call: the current code's audit line did not actually contain the tier, but the spec explicitly names the create audit line as something that recorded the tier and must now record the level. I followed the spec's explicit instruction and had it record `membershipLevel`. No test asserts the audit format either way, so this doesn't risk existing tests.",
